## Architecture Provenance

The decay-risk framework, Iron Law (Symptom → Source → Consequence → Remedy), Health
Score, and Mermaid dependency-graph approach used in this software are derived from
the open-source *brooks-lint* project (MIT License). Code Shine is a secondary
development that re-positions that architecture for the Codex CLI ecosystem and the
OpenAI SDK, and adds support for 20+ programming languages. The architecture itself is
a synthesis of widely-known software-engineering principles and is not copyrightable;
what is copyrightable is this specific expression, which is released under MIT above.
